{title: 337 - Redeemed!}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #337 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: A}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 337}
{meta: category Gospel - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[A]Redeemed, how I love to proclaim [E]it! Redeemed [A]by the blood of [G#dim]the Lamb;
[F#m]Redeemed through His infinite [A]mercy, His child and forever [E]I am.
[A]Redeemed, redeemed, [G#dim]Redeemed by the blood of the Lamb;
[A]Redeemed, redeemed, His child and forever I am.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[A]Redeemed, redeemed,
[A]Redeemed [G#dim]by the [F#m]blood of the Lamb;
[A]Redeemed, redeemed,
[A]His child and forever [D/A]I am.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[A]Redeemed, and so happy in Jesus,
[F#m]No language [A]my rapture can [E]tell;
[A]I know that [G#dim]the light of His presence
[A]With me doth continually dwell.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[A]I know there's a [E]crown that [A]is waiting
[F#m]In yonder [A]bright mansion for [E]me;
[A]And soon, with [G#dim]the spirit made perfect,
[A]At home with the Lord I shall be.
{end_of_verse}
